## Why This Is Asked
New angle: third-party feed integrity across regions; captures data lineage and external fault containment.

## Key Concepts
- CAPA data model with lineage; - region-aware lifecycle; - logs/traces integration; - metrics for containment; - RCA and canary plan.

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example CAPA data model outline
type CAPA = {
  id: string; region: string; feedId: string; version: string;
  evidenceUris: string[]; logTraceIds: string[]; t_incident: string; t_detected: string;
  containmentStatus: 'Identified'|'Contained'|'Investigated'|'Remediated'|'Verified'|'Closed';
  recurrenceRate?: number; mttr?: number;
};
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you simulate data-feed corruption to validate the canary rollout?
- What tamper-evident mechanisms would you add to the evidence store?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design end-to-end CAPA, including data models, state management, and safety-conscious rollout in a high-stakes, multi-region domain.

## Key Concepts
- CAPA data modeling and evidence linking
- Region-aware lifecycle and escalation
- Lightweight API for CAPA CRUD with traces
- Metrics for containment and recurrence
- RCA templates and canary rollout strategies

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal Express endpoint sketch
const express = require('express');
const app = express();
app.use(express.json());
app.post('/capa', (req, res) => {
  // validate and persist CAPA with linked traces
  res.status(201).send({ id: 'capa-123' });
});
```

